PS5 IW620: the tx power query no longer waits forever

When the IW620 firmware stops answering, woal_set_get_tx_power() waited without a limit (MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT) while
cfg80211 held the wiphy mutex. NetworkManager waits for that mutex while holding RTNL, so every network call on the
console hung and anything network-related froze. With MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT_TIMEOUT a dead firmware gives a timeout
instead, as for remain-on-channel (ps5-iw620-roc-bounded-wait.patch, #60) and the station queries in upstream's
ps5-iw620-rtnl-bounded-wait.patch. The request is freed as before: only a pending one is kept.

Found by PS5-CachyOS (abrocoma), whose patch makes the same change.
---
diff --git a/mlinux/moal_ioctl.c b/mlinux/moal_ioctl.c
index effcc10..66f8af0 100644
--- a/mlinux/moal_ioctl.c
+++ b/mlinux/moal_ioctl.c
@@ -1904,7 +1904,7 @@ mlan_status woal_set_get_tx_power(moal_private *priv, t_u32 action,
 				power_cfg, sizeof(mlan_power_cfg_t),
 				sizeof(mlan_power_cfg_t));
 
-	ret = woal_request_ioctl(priv, req, MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT);
+	ret = woal_request_ioctl(priv, req, MOAL_IOCTL_WAIT_TIMEOUT);
 	if (ret != MLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS)
 		goto done;
 
